{
  "schema": 1,
  "kind": "cli",
  "subsystem": "GNU bc arbitrary-precision calculator",
  "notes": "Each case runs `bc -q` with a program file written from the case's script. Results come from the real program; this suite has no expected values. Runtime-error cases are excluded on purpose: bc's diagnostics contain interpreter internals that an independent implementation cannot reproduce. Held-out cases are never shown to spec writers or implementers. Every script ends with quit so a non-interactive run terminates after the case instead of waiting on standard input.",
  "query": "arbitrary-precision expression evaluation: numeric representation and scale, arithmetic operators, comparisons, variables, arrays, functions, control flow, output conversion and builtins",
  "expected_observables": [
    "one line of result per evaluated expression on stdout",
    "division and modulus results follow the current scale and truncate the quotient toward zero",
    "negative operands follow bc sign rules for quotient and remainder",
    "the printed form uses the number's scale, including a leading decimal point below one",
    "assignment, arrays, user functions and loops update state visible to later expressions",
    "ibase and obase change input parsing and output conversion"
  ],
  "cases": [
